 138:./src/tftpserver.c ****   /* Specify the block number being ACK'd.
 139:./src/tftpserver.c ****    * If we are ACK'ing a DATA pkt then the block number echoes that of the DATA pkt being ACK'd (du
 140:./src/tftpserver.c ****    * If we are ACK'ing a WRQ pkt then the block number is always 0
 141:./src/tftpserver.c ****    * RRQ packets are never sent ACK pkts by the server, instead the server sends DATA pkts to the
 142:./src/tftpserver.c ****    * host which are, obviously, used as the "acknowledgement".  This saves from having to sEndTrans
 143:./src/tftpserver.c ****    * an ACK packet and a DATA packet for RRQs - see RFC1350 for more info.  */
